 B, with Trstena winning a decision on criteria. This gave him the gold medal, because the winner of Group A, Korean " [:a {:href "/athletes/59186"} "Kim Jong-Gyu"] ", was injured winning his final match against West German " [:a {:href "/athletes/58398"} "Fritz Niebler"] ", and could not compete in the gold medal match. Takada won bronze by defeating Canadian " [:a {:href "/athletes/57577"} "Ray Takahashi"] ", 12-0, winning his second Olympic medal eight years after his first. Through 2012, Trstena is the youngest ever male wrestling gold medalist."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Round Eliminated"] [:th {:data-toggle "tooltip", :data-placement "right", :data-original-title "Classification Points", :class "footnote"} "CP"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "277"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59416"} "Šaban Trstena"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/YUG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/YUG.png"}] "YUG"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "152"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59186"} "Kim Jong-Gyu"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/KOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/KOR.png"}] "KOR"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {:class "bib"} "146"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/59100"} "Yuji Takada"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/JPN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/JPN.png"}] "JPN"]] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} "–"] [:td {} [:span {: